{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <stddef.h>\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    float x;\\n    float y;\\n} Point;\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    char label;\\n    int length;\\n    float *coordinates;\\n} Group;\\n\\nvoid on_error() {\\n    printf(\\\"Invalid input file.\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(1);\\n}\\n\\nint parse_number_of_groups() {\\n    int n;\\n    if (scanf(\\\" n_groups=%d \\\", &n) != 1) on_error();\\n\\n    return n;\\n}\\n\\nPoint parse_point() {\\n    float x, y;\\n    if (scanf(\\\" (%f ,%f) \\\", &x, &y) != 2) on_error();\\n\\n    Point point;\\n    point.x = x;\\n    point.y = y;\\n\\n    return point;\\n}\\n\\nGroup parse_next_group() {\\n    char label;\\n    int length;\\n\\n    if (scanf(\\\" label=%c \\\", &label) != 1) on_error();\\n    if (scanf(\\\" length=%d \\\", &length) != 1) on_error();\\n\\n    Group group;\\n    group.label = label;\\n    group.length = length;\\n    group.coordinates = (float *)malloc(sizeof(float) * (size_t)length * 2);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\\n        Point point = parse_point();\\n        group.coordinates[i] = point.x;\\n        group.coordinates[(size_t)length + (size_t)i] = point.y;\\n    }\\n\\n    return group;\\n}\\n\\nint parse_k() {\\n    int k;\\n    if (scanf(\\\" k=%d \\\", &k) != 1) on_error();\\n\\n    return k;\\n}\\n\\nfloat euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(Point a, Point b) {\\n    return ((b.x - a.x) * ((b.x - a.x))) + ((b.y - a.y) * (b.y - a.y));\\n}\\n\\nint compare_for_sort(const void *a, const void *b) {\\n    return *(char *)a - *(char *)b;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/knn.h\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"Removing the stray patch marker in the header should let the integrated serial SoA and bounded max-heap candidate compile, retaining efficient top-k selection while the original-selection fallback preserves behavior for NaN distances.\",\"notes\":\"The supplied candidate failed compilation because src/knn.h had a leading '+' before the Point typedef. This experiment corrects that source typo; the controller should evaluate the complete program. OpenMP variants are omitted because the archived measurements were slower on this target.\",\"sources_kept\":[\"4e5248ae712349b9\",\"718bf7eca1eb4d80\"],\"transformations\":[\"Removed the accidental leading '+' from the Point typedef so the integrated source builds.\",\"Retained structure-of-arrays point storage and a serial bounded max-heap ordered by squared distance and encounter order.\",\"Retained the original selection fallback for NaN distances and the existing label padding and vote behavior.\"]}"}}
